  "$comment": "Task -> model chain. The router tries each model in order, skipping any whose key is not set (or that lacks a capability the call needs: vision, PDF), and falls back on errors. Workers AI needs no key and is last in every chain. Per model: provider, model id, capabilities (json: schema|object|prompt; vision; pdf and pdfMaxPages; thinking: none|optional|always; caching: auto|explicit|none and minCacheTokens; maxContext; maxOutput; temperature: false when the API refuses one) and prices in USD per million tokens (in, cachedIn, cacheWrite, out, reasoning; long/longAbove for prompt-length tiers). Per task: thinking off|low|medium|high, pdf (attach the source PDF where the model reads it), mediaResolution. External prices and limits are from each provider's docs on 2026-10-16 (dated links in docs/MODELS.md); Workers AI prices from https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/platform/pricing/ the same day. DeepSeek is priced at its peak rate (off-peak is half), so the ledger errs high. Gemini 3.8 Flash prices double on 2027-01-01: update them then. gateway: AI Gateway route per provider; null calls the provider directly (Z.ai has no built-in gateway provider; set it to custom-zai after creating that custom provider). Override at deploy time with the MODEL_ROUTES var (same shape; tasks and models are merged over these).",
